{"author":{"id":"746a4d30afc20b78119cb8ed7c194f988174fc252f0e9d9eb92022244ef86db3"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1781360752,"nonce":"FzdyKLwRvmm46KmJWCdA1ZPm81I=","metadata":{"github-id":"I_kwDOK4fCvM8AAAABFYH1Uw","github-url":"https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/issues/257","origin":"github"},"title":"BizzyBoat: record + bridge Garmin sidescan nadir_depth and water_temperature","message":"The Garmin sidescan driver now publishes two per-ping scalars that aren't recorded or bridged on BizzyBoat:\n\n- `~/nadir_depth` (`sensor_msgs/Range`) — bottom range from the down-look sub-header v1 (marine_tools #36).\n- `~/water_temperature` (`sensor_msgs/Temperature`) — transducer surface water temperature from the d807 telemetry frame (marine_tools #38). Confirmed against an AML CTD cast and the boat's SVS; corroborated by Garmin's spec (transducer fast-response thermistor, the scalar Garmin maps to N2K PGN 130312).\n\nFully resolved: `/bizzy/sensors/sidescan/garmin_sidescan/{nadir_depth,water_temperature}`.\n\n## Changes (boat side only — operator auto-receives)\n\n1. **`/**/sonar_logger`** record list (`config/bizzyboat.yaml`) — add both topics so the operational sonar bag captures depth + temperature alongside the imagery.\n2. **`/**/udp_bridge`** (`config/bizzyboat.yaml`, wifi + vpn) — bridge both to the operator for live SA (both tiny; throttle `nadir_depth` on the constrained VPN).\n3. **`record_sidescan_debug.sh`** — add both to the ad-hoc debug capture's topic list (it's meant to capture *all* driver topics; currently misses `nadir_depth` too).\n\nBoat needs `git pull` + driver rebuild (marine_tools jazzy) for the topics to exist; this PR makes them recorded + bridged once they do.\n\n---\n**Authored-By**: `Claude Code Agent`\n**Model**: `Claude Fable 5`","files":null}]}